WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.040
Even if you read through the Bible’s Old
Testament recently, or perhaps aren’t an

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.870
overtly religious person to begin with, you
most likely will have still heard the tale

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:10.870
of Noah’s Ark.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.330
Here’s a quick rundown before things get
all anomalous.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.060
God appears to a man named Noah, warning him
that he plans to unleash a flood.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:24.609
This disaster will engulf the entire Earth,
and allow the world a chance to begin anew,

00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:26.949
washed clean for a fresh start.

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:31.310
God tells Noah this as he has appointed him
to carry out a task ahead of the coming flood.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:37.719
This task was to gather two, a male and female,
of every possible type of animal, and ensure

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:41.030
that the creatures survived the coming flood.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:46.359
And so, Noah and his family did this, they
rounded up two of every animal from every

00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:52.500
species, and two by two they were herded onto
a huge wooden boat: Noah’s Ark.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.700
Now, granted it does seem pretty unfeasible
that one man and his family were able to gather

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.489
at least two of every animal in the entire
world.

00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:06.400
And yes, there currently exists no scientific
evidence that a simultaneous global flood

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.890
is possible, or that the boat described in
the Bible ever actually existed in the first

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:12.890
place.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:17.150
And lastly, we know what you’re probably
already thinking: Are we about to reveal that

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:21.530
this video’s SCP is the actual Ark that
Noah used to survive the flood?

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:27.510
Or was he maybe gifted some anomalous item
that allowed him to fit all the animals inside

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:28.510
it?

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:32.730
All good guesses, but no, that’s not where
we’re going with this.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:39.050
We only bring up Noah’s Ark because it’s
the perfect segue into the real topic of today’s

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.330
video: SCP-6008.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:46.201
So, let’s set the stage and turn our focus
away from the time of the Old Testament, to

00:01:46.201 --> 00:01:48.670
almost eighty years in our future.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:54.330
The year is 2100, New Year’s Day, and Planet
Earth is on the brink of destruction.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:59.910
At this time, SCP-6008 is the designation
given to the ongoing damage being done to

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:04.840
the environment, the threat of rising sea
levels caused by global warming.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:10.810
It is due to these inevitable disasters that
the SCP Foundation in their wisdom has realized

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:15.250
that a number of their containment facilities
and other sites are at risk of being destroyed

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.950
by environmental collapse.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.190
So, to combat this, what do they do?

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:25.780
Use some anomalous technology like SCP-2000
or a powerful, reality-warping entity to reverse

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.110
the damage done to the Earth?

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:33.020
No, they naturally start building facilities
in places that are higher up, and less likely

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:37.980
to be ruined by a climate disaster, as this
was a little more practical than taking the

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.450
anomalous nuclear option.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:45.460
Aware of the impending devastation the Foundation
and the world faced, the O5 Council found

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:50.110
themselves holding strategy conferences with
the Ethics Committee as well as O4 Command.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:55.390
Bear in mind, the O4s are a different team
within the Foundation than the O5 Council.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:00.850
The Council, as you are probably aware, are
the supreme overseers of the entire organization

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.770
with executive power over every facet of its
operation.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:07.010
Or at least, that’s their role in a nutshell.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:11.120
They also all happen to be immortal and have
been at the head of the SCP Foundation for

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.440
perhaps centuries, but let’s not stray too
far off-topic here.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.080
On the other hand, The O4 Command is almost
like a subdivision, whose function is to declare

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.680
and implement the lockdown of Foundation facilities.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:30.400
If a site is compromised, either by an SCP
breaching containment, or say, by an environmental

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:35.530
disaster, then O4 Command’s job is to declare
a lockdown, call in assistance from another

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:40.560
site, and otherwise carry out the proper security
protocols to handle the occurrence.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.170
The point of their conference was to determine
whether or not the SCP Foundation was within

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:50.069
its rights to use anomalous means to combat
the effects of climate change.

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:53.739
On the one side of the argument, from the
stance of the Ethics Committee, the Foundation

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:59.080
had a duty and responsibility to protect and
safeguard the people of Planet Earth.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.700
Unless they did something, humanity would
be doomed.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.580
The counterpoint was that the Foundation had
no right to interfere and change the fate

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.390
of the world on a whim.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.989
Not like they’ve ever done that before,
right?

00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:16.359
Ultimately, the O5 Council had the final say
and voted not to employ their anomalous resources

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:18.289
to prevent catastrophe.

00:04:18.289 --> 00:04:23.610
According to them, humanity had caused this
themselves and the SCP Foundation had no right

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.610
to interfere.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:29.210
Instead, they focused on protecting the organization
itself.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:34.689
Their relocation operation commenced in the
latter half of 2100, with all Foundation facilities

00:04:34.689 --> 00:04:39.520
in the north-eastern United States placed
in a near-permanent state of high alert.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.930
Twenty four anomalous breaches occurred, and
a total of sixteen Mobile Task Forces were

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:48.409
deployed to either re-contain these SCPs,
or eliminate them.

00:04:48.409 --> 00:04:53.270
All the while, with threats from the environment
looming ever closer, the Foundation’s Ethics

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.789
Committee was still pushing for something
to be done to help the civilians that would

00:04:56.789 --> 00:04:59.270
fall victim to the catastrophe.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:04.889
They drafted up plans and proposals to assist
some eleven billion refugees, but these were

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:07.659
once again rejected by Overwatch Command.

00:05:07.659 --> 00:05:13.599
Instead, their plan hinged on the activation
of SCP-2000, an underground Foundation facility

00:05:13.599 --> 00:05:18.440
designed to be used for the reconstruction
of human civilization following an XK-Class

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.240
end of the world scenario.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:26.729
In other words, it’s a human factory, capable
of recreating our entire species in the event

00:05:26.729 --> 00:05:29.210
of total global extinction.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:34.669
This drew the attention of one Ms. D.C. al
Fine, the Undersecretary of the Global Occult

00:05:34.669 --> 00:05:35.669
Coalition.

00:05:35.669 --> 00:05:40.409
Her intention was to act on behalf of the
GOC to directly intervene in the Foundation’s

00:05:40.409 --> 00:05:43.699
plans for the approaching environmental disasters.

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:48.029
However, certain members of the O5 Council
didn’t seem too open about sharing their

00:05:48.029 --> 00:05:52.889
strategies, claiming that the Foundation was
doing nothing to prevent the oncoming ecological

00:05:52.889 --> 00:05:57.379
apocalypse, nor did they have a contingency
in place.

00:05:57.379 --> 00:06:03.550
However, one of the council members, O5-12
otherwise known as Nakeda, approached Ms al

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.449
Fine shortly after this meeting.

00:06:05.449 --> 00:06:09.639
According to him, there were a number of the
council who shared al Fine’s sentiments,

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:14.219
that the Foundation’s resources could be
used to preserve human life, even if they

00:06:14.219 --> 00:06:17.309
could not be seen as preventing the end of
the world.

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:22.150
Nakeda took the opportunity to introduce al
Fine to something known only as the Genesis

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.530
Initiative.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:27.749
Over the course of the next year, mercenaries
working for the GOC attempted to steal a number

00:06:27.749 --> 00:06:30.620
of anomalies from the SCP Foundation.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.939
Their hands forced, the O5 Council ordered
the termination of ninety-eight percent of

00:06:34.939 --> 00:06:41.210
their contained entities and objects, and
in retaliation, MTF Alpha-1, the Red Right

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:44.860
Hand, was sent to hunt down the GOC leaders.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:51.169
Among the SCPs destroyed by GOC mercenaries
was SCP-2000, which wasn’t the Foundation’s

00:06:51.169 --> 00:06:56.499
secret contingency plan, but the backup in
case Nakeda’s Genesis Initiative failed.

00:06:56.499 --> 00:07:00.819
Or as he described it, a restart button for
the entire planet.

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:05.819
Al Fine had ordered SCP-2000s destruction,
hoping it would get the Genesis Initiative

00:07:05.819 --> 00:07:10.649
off the ground, forcing the O5 Council to
allow this plan to go forward.

00:07:10.649 --> 00:07:16.240
It was a tragedy of errors: Fine believed
that SCP-2000 was only a boot-up system for

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.870
the O5 Council, not all of humanity.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:24.749
Nakeda was unconvinced, claiming that humanity’s
only hope was something he referred to as

00:07:24.749 --> 00:07:26.199
Noah.

00:07:26.199 --> 00:07:27.220
And as for al Fine?

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:32.199
She went missing during the evacuation of
New York City, never appearing at any refugee

00:07:32.199 --> 00:07:35.419
sites, or ever even being spotted by facial
recognition.

00:07:35.419 --> 00:07:39.490
Who or what was the ‘Noah’ that Nakeda
had so much faith in?

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:45.020
Well, rather than its Biblical namesake, this
Noah wasn’t a person, but an artificial

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.280
intelligence.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:52.129
An AIC - or Artificially Intelligent Conscript
- for those who are not yet aware, is an advanced

00:07:52.129 --> 00:07:57.080
form of artificial intelligence that the Foundation
developed and uses to run its systems.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.539
So, what was the purpose of the Noah AIC?

00:08:00.539 --> 00:08:05.689
To protect the last living organisms on Planet
Earth, and complete the final stages of the

00:08:05.689 --> 00:08:07.659
Genesis Initiative.

00:08:07.659 --> 00:08:12.300
With the destruction of SCP-2000, countless
physical samples of the world’s genetic

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.979
history had been lost.

00:08:13.979 --> 00:08:19.939
DNA taken from every species of creature and
plant on Earth had been stored at the SCP-2000

00:08:19.939 --> 00:08:23.789
facility, and all of them were now destroyed.

00:08:23.789 --> 00:08:29.559
However, there did still exist a digital database,
containing the information on all of those

00:08:29.559 --> 00:08:31.300
genetic blueprints.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:36.240
It fell to the Noah AIC to come up with ways
that this data could be used to somehow save

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.469
the organisms of Planet Earth.

00:08:38.469 --> 00:08:42.909
The goal of the Genesis Initiative became
a race for the solution of how to use this

00:08:42.909 --> 00:08:49.880
information about the genetics of every species
to somehow recreate those species after the

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:50.890
world had ended.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:56.839
Or, to put it more plainly, this artificial
intelligence had to figure out how to 3D print

00:08:56.839 --> 00:08:58.889
all life on Earth.

00:08:58.889 --> 00:09:04.209
At this point, it had been over one hundred
years since the destruction of SCP-2000.

00:09:04.209 --> 00:09:09.060
The damage to the environment was not reversing
as some had hoped, and humanity was on its

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.620
last legs.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:15.690
During a routine life-extension procedure
being carried out by Noah, O5-12, Jonathan

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:20.160
Nakeda was much the same, nearing the end
of his extended lifespan.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:26.540
At two hundred and forty six, he was tired,
having lived longer than humans were naturally

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.540
meant to.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:32.880
And, perhaps due to cellular degradation over
many decades, or maybe just because he couldn’t

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:38.750
bear to continue, Jonathan passed away, on
September 13th 2204.

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:44.509
Over another hundred years later in 2367,
the Noah AIC was able to reawaken a version

00:09:44.509 --> 00:09:49.720
of Nakeda’s consciousness, a construct that
the AIC assembled from memories the Overseer

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:51.459
had scanned into Noah’s database.

00:09:51.459 --> 00:09:56.940
The artificial intelligence had hoped to call
on Nakeda’s advice one final time, only

00:09:56.940 --> 00:10:00.029
able to maintain the construct for a short
while.

00:10:00.029 --> 00:10:05.330
The AIC had come to realize that Earth was
a lost cause, humanity had all but dwindled

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:09.010
into extinction by this point, but Noah had
a plan.

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:13.860
It was able to generate nanoscale assembly
robots, essentially microscopic machines that

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:16.000
could be used to build things.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:20.509
Noah had activated Jonathan’s consciousness
construct to ask for permission, to divert

00:10:20.509 --> 00:10:25.490
all of its processing power into constructing
something that could, potentially, restore

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:29.480
humanity as well as all other life on the
now-dead Earth.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:34.940
It would take a long, long time to complete,
but perhaps the Genesis Initiative’s goals

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:40.259
were still driving Noah to strive for a solution,
even in the wake of extinction.

00:10:40.259 --> 00:10:45.339
When asked by the persistent AIC for permission
in setting its plan in motion, Jonathan answered

00:10:45.339 --> 00:10:49.029
from beyond the grave “We're all dead, my
friend.

00:10:49.029 --> 00:10:51.079
Do what you think is best.”

00:10:51.079 --> 00:10:58.610
So, all of this brings us back to the biggest
unanswered question: what even is SCP-6008?

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:03.050
What does this long, complex story have to
do with the story of Noah’s Ark?

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:07.399
Well, think about it for a moment, both stories
feature a natural disaster that threatens

00:11:07.399 --> 00:11:11.620
the entire world, every man, woman, and child.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:16.330
And Noah’s Ark was intended to preserve
life in the wake of the flood, and that is

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:19.949
the exact purpose of SCP-6008.

00:11:19.949 --> 00:11:25.170
It is a database, containing a history of
our entire species.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:27.990
Not just history, but the future as well.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:34.269
In fact, SCP-6008 has a digital record of
the genetic heritage of all life on Earth,

00:11:34.269 --> 00:11:37.110
every animal, plant, and person.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:41.950
It is held within a containment vessel appropriately
named Noah’s Ark, as it was built by the

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:45.720
AIC to travel through space towards a safe
haven.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.100
And what exactly was this safe haven?

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:55.070
A planetary system known by the designation
of TOI-178b, otherwise nicknamed ‘Jonathan’s

00:11:55.070 --> 00:12:01.790
Hope’, after Jonathan Nakeda, the O5 Council
member who had hoped humanity could be saved.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:05.810
The journey from Earth to Jonathan’s Hope
was over two hundred light years in distance,

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:11.060
but perhaps salvation would be waiting when
the Ark finally arrived, just like in the

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:12.600
Bible story.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:20.050
Under the watchful eye of the Noah AIC, SCP-6008
is set to reach its destination in over one

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:25.509
thousand years, when humanity can hopefully
begin again, without repeating the mistakes

00:12:25.509 --> 00:12:28.569
that drove them from Earth in the first place.

00:12:28.569 --> 00:12:33.320
And hopefully, we can get our act together
down here and stop things from getting worse,

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:36.839
before a future this bleak ever comes to be...

00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:42.699
Now go check out “Secret Group that Runs
the World - SCP O5 Council Explained” and

00:12:42.699 --> 00:12:47.300
“SCP-2000 - Deus Ex Machina” for more
of the groups and anomalies discussed in this

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:47.800
video!

